check into this submit run -- neither is part of the standing package
manifest, and lf52's L9 tail is known-broken live (confirmed this session:
HTTP 400 on an out-of-bounds coordinate). Submitting a known-broken sequence
as part of an irreversible leaderboard record would be worse than
submitting the safe, already-validated 60-level package.

Recorded the submission in ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml's live_submissions
history (fifth entry; first actual --submit since 2026-06-21).

